<p><b>Gnadira's Bio:</b>
<table border=1 width=400>
  <tr><td>
  There are moments in some people's lives of such stark clarity that they are forever changed, and not necessarily for the better. The Fudders of Ak'anon were an unusual family. There were four children in the family; Buck the eldest boy, Gneil and Gnormagn, the twin boys, and Gnadira the youngest and only daughter. Alone amongst the Fudder children, Gnadira was being raised like every other Gnome, not by rats like Gnormagn, not as some crazed Clockwork-making prodigy like Gneil, not as a fierce Warrior dedicated to cruel and intolerant behavior like Buck. Gnadira is the youngest member of the family, and as such was the apple of her father's eye. Their father, who did not realize his wife was a Priestess of Bertoxxulous, pampered his youngest in the way that Father's sometimes do with daughters. Gnadira's childhood was near idyllic before her Mother was caught by the authorities. That was years ago, her father's somewhat respectable position as a Clockwork Mechanic was ended because of his wife's membership in the dark reflection. Life became less than pleasant for Gneil and Buck, Buck became meaner, Gneil more eccentric. Gnormagn had been given to the Rats in infancy. Gnadira seemed untouch by the tragedy, people would say unkind things and she would take it in stride, they would talk about her mother behind her back and she would seem not to notice. SHe seemed under a delusion that everything would work out for the best. 

One day she had a dream. An older Gnome man in her dream told her to beware the King, and to fear the ticking Clockworks. Disturbed by this dream Gnadira began wandering Ak'anon looking at everything with a more critical eye. Through strange coincidence she wandered deep into the halls of the King, and learned the awful sobering truth, King Ak'anon is a Clockwork. It fractured her tiny mind. Looking at the shiny pieces of her shattered mind she saw her own reflection, a dark reflection, and she understood it all. The Clockworks don't serve Gnomes, they rule them, enslaving the Gnomes to service them and build new clockworks. Bertoxxulous didn't want to destroy Gnomish society, he wanted to free it. Free it from the Tyranny of the machine. Gnadira didn't know how it all started, but she knew how it was going to end. With King Ak'anon a rusted heap of useless gears at her feet and any of her poor misguided race who would stop her would choke on their own pus, bile and blood. She knew now what her mother strove for, and what she was preparing her children for. Gnadira also knew that a little girl cannot defeat a menace like this on her own, and she could not learn what she needed to know under the evere waking eye of the machines. She needed power and allies she could not forge in Ak'anon.
  </td></tr>
</table>



